# Markdown / OKF writing rules

Follow [Open Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.2](https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog/blob/main/okf/SPEC.md) for project docs. Keep docs Korean, concise, and structural (headings, lists, tables, fenced code)—not long prose.

## Concept documents (`docs/**/*.md` and other knowledge `.md`)

Every non-reserved `.md` SHOULD have YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
type: Reference          # REQUIRED — e.g. Reference, Playbook, Metric, Guide
title: 짧은 표시 제목
description: 한 줄 요약.
tags: [collector, backtest]
status: stable           # draft | stable | deprecated (absent ⇒ stable)
generated: { by: human:<id>, at: 2026-08-09T00:00:00Z }   # when known
---
```

- `type` is the only always-required key; unknown types are OK.
- Prefer `title`, `description`, `tags`. Use `resource` when the doc describes a concrete URI/path.
- Agent/human edits: set `generated.by` with actor form `human:<id>`, `<agent>/<version>`, or `process:<id>`.
- Optional provenance: `sources` with `resource` (+ optional `id` for footnotes). Attribute claims with `[^source-id]` footnotes keyed to `sources[].id`—no `# Citations` body list.
- Optional trust: `verified: { by: human:<id>, at: ... }`. Optional freshness: `stale_after: YYYY-MM-DD`.

### Body

- No required sections. Prefer clear `#` / `##` headings, tables for schemas/options, fenced commands for CLI.
- Cross-links: prefer **bundle-root absolute** paths (`[흐름](/docs/flow.md)`). Relative links are OK. Broken links are tolerated (not-yet-written).
- End investment-related docs with: `투자 조언을 제공하지 않습니다.` when the doc discusses market data or backtests.

### Reserved filenames

Do not use these names for normal concepts:

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `index.md` | Directory listing (progressive disclosure); usually **no** frontmatter except root may have `okf_version: "0.2"` |
| `log.md` | Chronological updates, newest first, `## YYYY-MM-DD` headings |

`index.md` entry style:

```markdown
# 섹션

* [제목](relative.md) - frontmatter description 한 줄
```

## Root `README.md`

MAY stay a thin command cheat-sheet **without** full OKF frontmatter. Point to `docs/` for detail. Do not duplicate long pipeline docs in README.

## Do / Don't

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD: freeform wall of text, no type, positional "see above" -->
이 문서는 수집 방법을 설명합니다. 위에서 말한 대로 실행하세요.

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
---
type: Guide
title: 데이터 흐름
description: CLI에서 curated 저장까지의 파이프라인.
tags: [collector]
status: stable
---

# CLI

| 명령 | 역할 |
|------|------|
| `market-data update` | 미수집 1일 갱신 |

자세한 가정은 [토이 백테스트](/docs/backtest.md)를 보세요.
```

- Do not invent Attested Computation / executor / attester unless the doc is literally a sanctioned computation.
- Do not reject or rewrite docs solely for missing optional OKF fields; add them when creating or substantially editing.
- Prefer updating `docs/README.md` index links when adding a new doc under `docs/`.
